712: ### 3d. Applied AFTER table 2, comment-only: the first seat's one L4 correction (CHECK IT -- a correction is not safer than what it corrects)
713: 
714: The shipped probe's ORDER DEPENDENCE paragraph stated PRETABLE2's prediction (a bit-3 collision) as this build's
715: behaviour, while table 2 measured the other shape (section 4's MISS note).  No code line changed; the frozen copy table 2
716: ran keeps the old text because it is the text that ran.
717: 
718: ```diff
719: --- rev3 as table 2 ran it (md5 ddcebfe3)
720: +++ rev3 as shipped now (md5 346c7813)
721: @@ -195,5 +195,8 @@
722:  ORDER DEPENDENCE: a latch shift that loses its 64-bit literal (`1ULL' -> `1u') is undefined behaviour at MISC's bit
723: -35; on this x86-64 build it lands on bit 3, SLAVELMOD2's (0x0c), and `p2 ann rd' / `p2 ann wr' reach 0x0c before
724: -0x8c in POP2 order, so MISC's announce is silenced -- a reorder of POP2 can move that kill (table 2 records the
725: -host and the row).
726: +35, so what it does is the compiler's choice.  This paragraph said "on this x86-64 build it lands on bit 3,
727: +SLAVELMOD2's (0x0c) ... so MISC's announce is silenced"; that was PRETABLE2's prediction, and kill table 2 measured
728: +the alternative PRETABLE2 named instead: GCC 15.2.1 -O3 specialised the MISC case and folded the shift to 0, so
729: +MISC never latches -- 27 lines in pass 1 and 2 in pass 2, red `p2 ann rd', `p2 ann wr' and both `2' rows
730: +(killtable2_20261021/obj/M_ONENARROW_codegen.txt).  The masked-count shape (bit 3, MISC silenced behind 0x0c in
731: +POP2 order, so a reorder of POP2 could move the kill) was not built.  No portable claim.
732:  
733: @@ -247,3 +250,4 @@
734:  ZERO_OFF = 0x30             # `p2 zero wr': DMACTL -- its own session; not MISC (0x8c) and not SLAVELMOD2 (0x0c),
735: -                            # the pair a 32-bit latch shift collides on x86-64, and no non-census session touches it
736: +                            # the pair a 32-bit latch shift could collide (undefined; see ORDER DEPENDENCE), and no
737: +                            # non-census session touches it
738:  LANE0_HU = 0xb0             # `p1 widths': a word-aligned (lane-0) halfword start no other access there uses
739: ```
