  * the population-2 arm vs #501's PCC2 `default:' (latched fatal, direction decides wording, `(once)'): rev 3
    adds the zero-valued first store (`p2 zero wr': direction decides the wording even when the value is 0) and
    the cross-width latch hold (`p2 nw rd 2' / `p2 nw wr 2': a non-word first access latches).
  * `default:' vs dev_unreadable.c (pure FAULT): both `return 0'; no asymmetry owed (unchanged from PRETABLE.out).
  * the population-2 arm vs itself across lanes (FB F10c): word starts are labels, sub-word starts fault; `p1
    widths' now holds BOTH lane-0 widths in population 1 (ld.hu 0xb0, st.b 0xb4) beside the lane-1/2/3 accesses.

== 2. CLAIM -> ROW (every comment sentence fix568b ADDS or REWRITES over HEAD; RECORDED: the added comment text) ==
  RECORDED (78 lines added or rewritten over HEAD, 31 of them comment text; fix568b line numbers):
      55 |     /*  #568: one bit per register WORD (relative_addr >> 2) for the
      56 |         unimplemented-register announce below; the highest such word is
      57 |         VME2_MISC (0x8c >> 2 == 35).  Zeroed by DEVINIT's memset, so every
      58 |         instance starts with every announce armed.  */
      62 | /*  #568: a warned_unimpl narrower than VME2_MISC >> 2 + 1 bits would
