      65 |     below is not checked here.  */
     150 |     /*  #568 (vmedefaultkill): registers the header names but this model
     151 |         does not implement.  Each ended the emulator in default: below.
     152 |         OpenBSD 2.2's mvme88k driver (sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c) has
     153 |         access sites at six of them.  Its attach reaches four:
     154 |         vme2chip_init() reads MASTERCTL and writes it back and writes
     155 |         MASTER3, MASTER4 and MASTER4MOD.  The other two, IRQSTAT and
     156 |         IRQCLR, are in vme2abort(), the ABORT-switch interrupt handler,
     157 |         and this model raises no VME2 interrupt.  A bus error here
     158 |         would panic that guest's attach, so these DECLINE: a read is served
     159 |         the word preloaded above, which is 0 because nothing writes these
     160 |         words of d->reg[] (odata is deliberately not forced to 0, so a store
     161 |         added by a later edit would show in a read-back); a write is
     162 |         dropped; one fatal() per register per device, the first access's
     163 |         direction deciding its wording (#501's shape in dev_pcc2.c).
     164 |         Sub-word starts inside these words are not matched here and reach
     165 |         default: (vmewidthlanes).  */
     213 |         /*  #568 (vmedefaultkill): an offset this model does not service:
     214 |             no header-named register, or the inside of one (a sub-word
     215 |             start).  Refuse the access -- for a guest data load or store,
     216 |             memory_rw then raises the m88k data-access exception, the bus
     217 |             error a badaddr() probe expects -- instead of exit(1), which
     218 |             ended the emulator with no visible reason (debug() is silent
     219 |             at default verbosity).  */
  CLAIMS and their rows:
    - struct: one bit per register WORD ... Zeroed by DEVINIT's memset, so every instance starts with every announce armed
        -> p2 ann rd / p2 ann wr (26 first-access lines each), p2 nw rd / p2 nw wr, p2 zero wr
    - typedef: a warned_unimpl narrower than VME2_MISC >> 2 + 1 bits ... make that a compile error
        -> NO RUNTIME ROW, by construction: leg M_CAPNARROW must FAIL TO BUILD
    - typedef: The 1ULL in the shifts below is not checked here
        -> a DISCLOSURE; leg M_ONENARROW measures what that literal's narrowing does on this host (UB-mediated)
    - arm: registers the header names but this model does not implement. Each ended the emulator in default: below
        -> HEAD (test-first): the 20 population rows die on HEAD
    - arm: OpenBSD 2.2's mvme88k driver has access sites at six of them. Its attach reaches four ... IRQSTAT and IRQCLR ... ABORT-switch interrupt handler, and this model raises no VME2 interrupt
        -> NO ROW: a SOURCE-READING claim about the guest (no mvme187 OpenBSD boot image on this host; GLM's boot census offered, not adopted); NOT CLAIMED in the probe contract
    - arm: A bus error here would panic that guest's attach
        -> NO ROW: counterfactual about a guest boot; NOT CLAIMED
    - arm: a read is served the word preloaded above, which is 0 ... (odata is deliberately not forced to 0, so a store added by a later edit would show in a read-back)
        -> p2 rd census, p2 ld widths (0 served); p2 wr census, p2 st widths (a store shows: M_STORE)
    - arm: a write is dropped
        -> p2 wr census, p2 st widths
    - arm: one fatal() per register per device, the first access's direction deciding its wording
