VERDICT: the objects are NOT identical apart from the read announce.  The only SOURCE-semantic change is D1 -- the
read announce's format (`0x%x' -> `0x%llx') and cast (`(unsigned)' -> `(unsigned long long)' odata) -- and the
object differs in THREE further ways:
  (1) devinit_vme: `push $0xe7' -> `push $0xea' -- __LINE__ 231 -> 234.  DEVINIT's CHECK_ALLOCATION expands to
      FAILURE(), which passes __FILE__, __LINE__ and __func__ (src/include/misc.h); fix568b's comment rewrites add three
      lines above it (reach comment +2, default: comment +1).  A COMMENT-ONLY edit changes this object.
  (2) dev_vme_access: the cast makes odata a 64-bit argument (`mov %r14,%rcx' into the read announce's fatal()),
      and GCC's register allocation, block layout and tail duplication change with it: temporaries swap rdi<->rsi,
      alignment nops differ, two branches flip polarity, and the read-announce call path is DUPLICATED (fatal() call
      sites 2 -> 3 and read-announce format references 1 -> 2, counted by string content) -- .text 1890 -> 1970 bytes.
  (3) .rodata.str1.x: the read format string itself, and the string pool's ORDER (the default: arm's two debug()
      strings now follow the two announce strings).
  (2) and (3) are compiler consequences of D1; (1) is a consequence of comment line counts.  No other source change
  exists (rev3/dev_vme.fix568b.c vs fix568: the typedef rewrite, three comment rewrites, the format and the cast).

